    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: deterministic `householdId`\n\nThe household is now keyed purely on `(lastName, postcode)`, and everything that keys off the household derives from a single computed value.\n\n**`Household.java`** \u2014 Rewrote to a deterministic derivation: `householdId` = first **12 upper-hex characters** of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (last name trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased; postcode trimmed). Added `idFor(request)` / `idFor(owner)` overloads and a `sharesHousehold(request)` helper. Removed the old opt-in/link-creating logic (`resolveId`, `assign`, member write-back).\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 Now *always* stamps the computed id (`owner.setHouseholdId(Household.idFor(owner))`), regardless of `sharesHousehold`, so owners with the same last name + postcode share it automatically.\n\n**`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java`** (the duplicate block) \u2014 Now rejects with **409** when any existing owner has the same computed `householdId`. A request that sets `sharesHousehold` **bypasses** this block and is created as a declared member.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 A declared household member (`sharesHousehold` true) is explicitly **not** flagged as a possible duplicate (flags left false/absent); otherwise the existing soft-match logic is unchanged.\n\n**`OwnerIdentityKey.java`** \u2014 `forRequest` now uses the computed household id (dropped the now-unused repository param); `forOwner` (used by the response mapper) unchanged.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 Updated `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` and the OpenAPI descriptions for `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, `identityKey`, and `possibleDuplicate` to match the new semantics.\n\n## Behaviour verification\n\nThe one existing/new test \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` \u2014 passes, along with the full suite (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, BUILD SUCCESS`). It confirms same last name + postcode \u2192 same `householdId`, a different last name \u2192 a different one, the second same-household owner is accepted via `sharesHousehold`, and the first owner needs no opt-in to get an id.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: this arm's membership level derives from `namesakeCount` and email (per its OpenAPI schema), not a household-size input \u2014 so there was no household-size-to-membership wiring to redirect here; the spec's mention of it doesn't correspond to code in this codebase.",
